 "result": "\n\nFixed. One-line change in the seed: the parent issue `i-web-5` (\"Checkout revamp: payment form overhaul\", assigned to Dana) moved from cycle 42 to the Web team's previous cycle 41.\n\n- **Why this fix:** `i-web-5` previously matched \"Checkout revamp project\" and \"cycle 42 of the Web team\", so it failed only the assignee condition — an undeclared near miss. It now fails two conditions (assignee is Dana; it's in cycle 41), so a reader who resolves any one condition correctly excludes it.\n- **Why not declare it instead:** declaring it would have required a third `R:Issue.assigneeId` decoy outside the designated substitute menu (plain \"different assignee\"), which is weaker than the menu decoys already present.\n- **No ripple damage:** `i-web-5` stays in the Checkout revamp project, so the `i-web-4` decoy (project inherited from parent) still works; it's assigned to Dana, so the title-based `i-web-7` decoy mutation still selects only `i-web-7`. All six decoy mutations still select their witnesses, and the reference query still selects only the target `i-web-1`.\n\nNo wording changed; the request is untouched.",
